["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"service-sdk","stream_identity":"01a0cabb-b0b0-7507-816e-f5963e5d4c1d","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIG8516a5e075bbb72cbc732a24c4033d38d29bc765e9f31fafca3ad2176782bf01","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/service-console-theme-contract","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":4,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"## Outcome\n\nEvery generated service console inherits a host product's semantic theme without knowing that product's preference model, while standalone generated documentation remains accessible by default.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- The Vue console consumes a documented optional `--b10x-*` CSS token contract for canvas, surfaces, text, borders, accent, status, focus, code, overlays, and elevation.\n- Every token has a neutral system-aware fallback, so standalone generated documentation needs no host theme dependency.\n- The console accepts no Devcenter-specific theme prop, reads no host storage, and branches on no named product theme.\n- Host token overrides style operation navigation, forms, lifecycle/views, activity results, focus, and native controls without leaking outside the widget.\n- TypeScript, widget, generated-docs, Rust, and AEP gates pass.\n","relations":[{"derived_from":"epic:builder-runtime"},{"serves":"vision:composable-services"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"Let generated service consoles inherit documented semantic host tokens while retaining accessible standalone defaults.","title":"Make generated consoles themeable"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"}},"id":"MIG8516a5e075bbb72cbc732a24c4033d38d29bc765e9f31fafca3ad2176782bf01","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":4,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIG8516a5e075bbb72cbc732a24c